---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Shot from '../../components/Shot.astro';
import Chart from '../../components/Chart.astro';
import Stats from '../../components/Stats.astro';
import HeadLinks from '../../components/HeadLinks.astro';
import { u } from '../../lib/url';
import '../../styles/brandbook.css';
import '../../styles/sidequest.css';

const demo = 'https://usqr.github.io/font-analysis-app/';
const repo = 'https://github.com/usqr/font-analysis-app';
const origin = 'https://useratio.com/the-anatomy-of-a-thousand-typefaces/app/';
const article = 'https://medium.com/@getflourish/the-anatomy-of-a-thousand-typefaces-f7b9088eed1';

const sections = [
  { id: 'story', title: 'Story' },
  { id: 'look', title: 'How it looks' },
  { id: 'history', title: 'History' },
  { id: 'tags', title: 'Tags from the outlines' },
  { id: 'features', title: 'What it does' },
  { id: 'try', title: 'Try it' },
] as const;
const num = (i: number) => String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0');

const stats = [
  ['Fonts in the demo', '3,569'],
  ['Font families', '1,994'],
  ['Commits', '48'],
  ['Serif or sans correct', '97.6%'],
] as const;

const history = [
  ['16 Mar 2026', 'First version: the scan, the glyph analysis as a picture, and the compare panel. On the same day: classification from the names, stars, saved folders, and manual categories that stay after a rescan.'],
  ['17 Mar 2026', 'The server calculates the analysis at scan time and keeps it in a database. Google Fonts come in with the analysis already done. Script detection, library filters, and variable fonts with axis sliders.'],
  ['18 Mar 2026', 'New gallery tiles with controls for variable fonts. Then a pause of eight months.'],
  ['18–19 Nov 2026', 'A static build of the Google Fonts set goes to GitHub Pages, so anyone can try it. Node 26 LTS. Tags from the glyph outlines, a slab filter, and tooltips.'],
  ['20 Nov 2026', 'I made mockups for the library, analyze, and compare views in Open Design and applied them. The end-to-end tests changed with the views. A review found small defects, and I fixed them.'],
] as const;

const days = [
  { label: '16 Mar', value: 9 },
  { label: '17 Mar', value: 7 },
  { label: '18 Mar', value: 1 },
  { label: '…', value: 0 },
  { label: '18 Nov', value: 1 },
  { label: '19 Nov', value: 14 },
  { label: '20 Nov', value: 16 },
];

const accuracy = [
  { label: 'File metadata', value: 76.4 },
  { label: 'Glyph outlines', value: 97.6 },
];

const features = [
  ['Library', 'Scan local folders recursively, or browse the Google Fonts set. Fonts are grouped by family, with live previews.'],
  ['Filters', 'Range filters with histograms for contrast, weight, width, and x-height, plus category, script, style count, and variable fonts.'],
  ['Analyze', 'Stroke contrast, x-height, proportions, weight, spacing, and a glyph grid for each font. Export the results as JSON or as an image.'],
  ['Compare', 'Put several fonts on one canvas with their metrics lines, with an option to normalize the x-height.'],
  ['Variable fonts', 'Sliders for each axis, with a short explanation of more than 20 standard axes.'],
  ['Classification', 'Automatic categories from names, PANOSE, and the glyph shapes. Manual changes stay after a full rescan.'],
] as const;
---
<Base title="Font analysis app" current="sidequests" description="A library for font files: scan folders, measure each font, and find fonts by x-height, contrast, weight, and width.">
  <div class="wrap bb">
    <header class="page-head mgrid">
      <div class="m"><p class="kicker"><span class="usq" aria-hidden="true"></span>Sidequest</p><p class="count"><a href={u('/sidequests/')}>All sidequests</a></p></div>
      <div>
        <h1>Font analysis app</h1>
        <p class="lede">A library for font files. It scans folders, measures each font, and lets me find and compare fonts by their x-height, contrast, weight, and width.</p>
        <HeadLinks links={[['Open the live demo', demo], ['Source on GitHub', repo]]} />
      </div>
    </header>

    <section class="sec mgrid" id="story" aria-labelledby="story-h">
      <div class="sec-head sub"><span class="num m" aria-hidden="true">{num(0)}</span><h2 id="story-h">{sections[0].title}</h2></div>
      <div class="bb-flow">
        <p>The app <a href={origin}>The Anatomy of a Thousand Typefaces</a> gives more insight into fonts: it lets you find a font by its x-height. Its author, Florian Schulz, described the method in <a href={article}>an article on Medium</a>. I wanted to make my own version for some time.</p>
        <p>My earlier tries stopped at a wall. Sometimes the scope at the start was too large. Sometimes the AI tools invented results.</p>
        <p>This time I started small. The first version only showed the analysis of the glyphs as a picture. I had to see that the measurements were real, and not a product of the imagination of the app.</p>
        <p>Then I debugged it and expanded it, one step at a time. At this time it is a library: it scans folders recursively, analyzes fonts in bulk, and shows the details and comparisons. I spent a bit more time on it than I planned.</p>
        <dl class="bb-facts">
          <div><dt>Started</dt><dd>March 2026</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Stack</dt><dd>React 19, Express 5, opentype.js, Vite, TypeScript</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Formats</dt><dd>TTF, OTF, WOFF, WOFF2</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Tests</dt><dd>node:test and Playwright, also for the static build</dd></div>
        </dl>
      </div>
      <Stats items={stats} />
    </section>

    <section class="sec mgrid" id="look" aria-labelledby="look-h">
      <div class="sec-head sub"><span class="num m" aria-hidden="true">{num(1)}</span><h2 id="look-h">{sections[1].title}</h2></div>
      <p class="bb-note">Screenshots of the live demo, November 2026.</p>
      <Shot src="/sidequests/font-analysis/library.avif" width={1440} height={900}
        alt="The library view with the Slab category filter on: a grid of 70 slab serif families, and filters with histograms for contrast and weight."
        title="Library" caption="The Slab filter shows 132 fonts in 70 families. The asterisk marks a tag from the glyph outlines. The histograms show how the fonts spread over contrast and weight." />
      <Shot src="/sidequests/font-analysis/analyze.avif" width={1440} height={900}
        alt="The analyze view for Playfair Display: the letters o and O with the thickest and thinnest strokes marked, and a results table."
        title="Analyze" caption="Playfair Display has a contrast of 4.87 : 1 in the “o”. The app finds the thickest stroke (blue) and the thinnest stroke (red) on the outline." />
      <Shot src="/sidequests/font-analysis/compare.avif" width={1440} height={900}
        alt="The compare view with Lato, Roboto Slab, and Bitter on top of each other, with metrics lines and a table of metrics."
        title="Compare" caption="Lato, Roboto Slab, and Bitter on one baseline: the type of this site and its earlier serif. The table gives the metrics in font units." />
    </section>

    <section class="sec mgrid" id="history" aria-labelledby="history-h">
      <div class="sec-head sub"><span class="num m" aria-hidden="true">{num(2)}</span><h2 id="history-h">{sections[2].title}</h2></div>
      <div class="bb-flow">
        <p>The app grew in two short bursts of work, eight months apart.</p>
        <dl class="bb-facts">
          {history.map(([when, text]) => <div><dt>{when}</dt><dd>{text}</dd></div>)}
        </dl>
      </div>
      <Chart caption="Commits for each day of work" unit="commits" data={days} mark={[0, 6]}
        note="17 commits in March and 31 commits in November, in 7 pull requests. Nothing between them." />
    </section>

    <section class="sec mgrid" id="tags" aria-labelledby="tags-h">
      <div class="sec-head sub"><span class="num m" aria-hidden="true">{num(3)}</span><h2 id="tags-h">{sections[3].title}</h2></div>
      <div class="bb-flow">
        <p>Font files often have a wrong category, or none. So the app reads the outline of the letter “H”. If it finds serifs, the font is a serif. If the serifs are thick and flat, the font is also a slab.</p>
        <p>Script and decorative faces do not have a regular “H”. For them, the app keeps the category from the file. This rule cut the wrong labels on these faces from 162 to 53.</p>
      </div>
      <Chart kind="bars" caption="Serif or sans: correct labels on 1,029 Google font families" unit="%" suffix="%" data={accuracy} mark={[0, 1]}
        note="The reference is the category in the Google Fonts metadata. For slab detection, precision is 68% and recall is 65%, but the reference list of slabs is not complete." />
    </section>

    <section class="sec mgrid" id="features" aria-labelledby="features-h">
      <div class="sec-head sub"><span class="num m" aria-hidden="true">{num(4)}</span><h2 id="features-h">{sections[4].title}</h2></div>
      <div class="bb-flow">
        <dl class="bb-facts">
          {features.map(([name, text]) => <div><dt>{name}</dt><dd>{text}</dd></div>)}
        </dl>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="sec mgrid" id="try" aria-labelledby="try-h">
      <div class="sec-head sub"><span class="num m" aria-hidden="true">{num(5)}</span><h2 id="try-h">{sections[5].title}</h2></div>
      <div class="bb-flow">
        <p><a href={demo}>Open the live demo</a>. It is a static build with the Google Fonts set only. Your stars, categories, and tags stay in your browser.</p>
        <p>To scan your own font folders, run the app on your computer. <a href={repo}>Read the source on GitHub</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
